3) What is a dimension table
=============================

assume that you are a area sales manager and intrested to know how the sales are going.

somebody mentioned to you that yes today we soled 10,000 units of several products

just the number 10,000 doesn't add any value so we really can't understand wheather we are doing good or bad and what is the room for improvement.

this is where we need some context by which this number 10,000 can be divided.

so we will natureally ask questions like.

if my today's sale is 10,000 , how much was the sale yesterday?
what are my top 5 products?
what are my top 3 stores?
who are my top 10 customers?

the entities by which we divide the data becomes the dimensions and the measurement itself is the fact.

like.

customer:
id, name, address
product:
product_id,product_name,type
date:
order_Date,shipment_Date,delivery_date

dimensions will answer 7 questions.

who
what
when
where
why
how
how many

